# Notation

The following abbreviations will be used in the following slides

- nat = national
- for = foreign
- nc = national currency
- fc = foreign currency 

# The law of one price

- It states that in a competitive market, identical goods must have the same price. It follows that:
	- a person incurs the same purchase cost regardless of the seller from whom he intends to buy.

- In International Economics: a person bears the same cost regardless of the country in which he intends to purchase the asset

$$\underbrace{P^i_{nat}}_{\substack{price \\ in \ nc \\ of \\ nat \\ good}}=\underbrace{\underbrace{E_{nc/fc}}_{\substack{\text{quantity} \ of \ nc \\ per \ 1 \ \text{unit} \ di \ fc }} \times \underbrace{P^i_{for}}_{\substack{Price \ in \\ fc \ of \\ foreign \\ good}}}_{price \ in \ nc \ of \ foreign \ good}$$


# Examples

- For an American we have
$$\underbrace{P^i_{US}}_{\substack{price \\ in \ \$ \\ of \\ US \\ good}}=\underbrace{\underbrace{E_{\$/euro}}_{\substack{\text{quantity} \ of \ \$ \\ per \ 1 \ euro }} \times \underbrace{P^i_{for}}_{\substack{Price \ in \\ euro \ of \\ EU \\ good}}}_{price \ in \ nc \ of \ EU \ good}$$

